  "content": {
    "title": "Luke Combs to play Allegiant Stadium as 70,000 expected amid extreme heat warning",
    "text": "LAS VEGAS (KSNV) — Luke Combs is set to take the stage at Allegiant Stadium on Saturday, March 21, with an estimated crowd of about 70,000 fans expected for what could be one of the largest live events of the year in Las Vegas.With heavy demand anticipated for parking, rideshare and stadium entry, guests are strongly encouraged to plan ahead, arrive early and allow extra time to get inside. Heavy traffic is expected on roadways around Allegiant Stadium before and after the event.An extreme heat warning has been issued by the National Weather Service for the Las Vegas area, and fans walking to the stadium are urged to plan ahead and take precautions.Stadium gates are scheduled to open at 5 p.m., with showtime set for 5:50 p.m. Fans are encouraged to arrive well in advance of showtime to avoid peak congestion.SPORTS: NBA sets sights on Las Vegas & Seattle expansion & Aviators hold 2026 Media DaySecurity and entry policies will be enforced, including Allegiant Stadium’s clear bag policy. Any bag that does not comply will be denied entry. Approved bags must be clear plastic, vinyl or PVC and may not exceed 12 inches by 6 inches by 12 inches. Small clutch bags, purses or wallets measuring 4.5 inches by 6.5 inches by 2 inches or smaller are permitted.Allegiant Stadium will offer three bag check locations. There is a $20 non-refundable charge per bag, and payment is cashless.After the concert, guests are encouraged to allow extra time when exiting the stadium. More event information is available at www.allegiantstadium.com.",
